\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Wall--clock time per forward pass (ms), batch size $1$, $d = 64$, $K = 3$. All three DTFN variants scale (approximately) linearly to $16{,}384$ tokens. Numbers are from an Apple M4 CPU (MPS backend). The \emph  {scaling trend} (linear in $L$) is backend--independent because the DTFN forward pass is $\mathcal  {O}(L K d)$; an Ascend ASI3 NPU port is left to future work.}}{21}{table.16}\protected@file@percent }
